{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost","id":298980,"title":"\u200bHow Seasons communicate with the Lost?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-01T09:15:58-07:00","id":298980,"title":"\u200bHow Seasons communicate with the Lost?","content":"Question is in the topic. How Season is selecting it\u2019s Monarch to represent in freehold? How changelings can \u201ctalk\u201d with it\u2019s Court Season... being? Are Seasons Hedge bound True Fae or very powerful Hobgoblins?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m asking as I will run episodic game located in fictions small town in New England and I don\u2019t much see there many changelings beside players. To be frank, I can\u2019t imagine other Lost than player characters in the town of almost 2500 people. So I need a way to make PCs members of Courts without need of other changelings - because I <b>love</b> Seasonal Courts! Simplest solution it would be that Seasons themselves choose them. It could be Seasons agents to come to characters, if themselves don't see changelings from time to time - but who would work them? Specific Hobgoblins?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m using here a bit the similar <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/121131-using-the-firstborn?p=122010#post122010\">fan idea as with Firstborns of <b>Forsaken</b> that come from time to time and guide new werewolves in to they Tribes</a>, even without other Uratha to teach them in the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-04-2014, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T11:17:34-07:00","id":299109,"title":"","content":"There are a couple of options to choose from. <br /> <br /> 1: The seasons as entities have no direct hand in the process. Members of the court elect their King, or the previous season's monarch chooses who to hand the crown off to, or whoever can take the crown first keeps it.<br /> <br /> 2: The season automatically chooses the monarch, but the people involved must consent. Once the crown is granted, it must be given up by an act of will, whereupon it disappears and immediately appears upon the head of the next monarch, who may deny it if he wishes.<br /> <br /> 3: The season chooses, no matter what. The crown passes from person to person without any Changeling input, chosen by some arcane method the Changelings only vaguely understand. On the appropriate day, the Crown simply disappears from the previous monarch's head and appears on the head of the new monarch. A monarch must make an act of will or magic in order to try to claim an eternal monarchy like in Miami.<br /> <br /> 4: The Seasons possess avatars, either voices or physical forms which appear in order to enact their will. Summer's avatar, for example, is The Burning Man, a figure all of white-hot flame, while Winter's is a wraith of freezing-cold wind. <br /> <br /> I personally am not a huge fan of option 4, as it makes the seasonal entities too accessible. In my games, it's generally some combination of 1-3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T12:23:39-07:00","id":299181,"title":"","content":"I more or less agree with Hobbitguy here. The crown appearing seems to be a thing that happens, but choosing monarchs also seems to be a thing that happens. Seasons don't seem to speak so much as pop a crown on someone. I'd go with 1, 2, or 3, or some combination. I tend to go with a sort of combo of 1 and 2, in the sense who people choose seems to influence it, but the crown ultimately just appears to be kept or denied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T12:55:31-07:00","id":299200,"title":"","content":"Just a question, if there is only one Summer Courtier in a city, she does not have to manifest a crown? I think that would go against my character concept, at least at a beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T13:27:37-07:00","id":299240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=299200#post299200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a question, if there is only one Summer Courtier in a city, she does not have to manifest a crown? I think that would go against my character concept, at least at a beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's only one changeling sworn to Summer in a given city, <i>you do not have a Summer Court.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T13:35:39-07:00","id":299243,"title":"","content":"Eh, my bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T14:05:12-07:00","id":299259,"title":"","content":"True question of the topic: <b>If in my town I don't have any other changelings - could character learn from the Season itself how to join to it? Or maybe some Season agent, like Hobgoblin in the service of Spring?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=299240#post299240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's only one changeling sworn to Summer in a given city, <i>you do not have a Summer Court.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And from what number there is Summer Court? Because, you know, in city there is one member of the Court, so theoretically he could be Summer Monarch. Even if he would only rule himself. Are there any official rulings in the game line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T16:16:41-07:00","id":299441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=299259#post299259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True question of the topic: <b>If in my town I don't have any other changelings - could character learn from the Season itself how to join to it? Or maybe some Season agent, like Hobgoblin in the service of Spring?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The very first supplement in the line addressed this very question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rogue Changelings and the Courts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In most freeholds, the Courts as mystical pledges between an individual changeling and a season and the Courts as social and political entities made up of changelings all sworn to the same season are synonymous. When a changeling joins the Summer Court, for example, she swears her fealty to Summer by proxy when she makes her pledge to the [Summer] King. Thereafter, she is a member of the Summer Court in both the mystic and the political sense.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t always the case, however. While certainly a more difficult prospect, it isn\u2019t entirely unreasonable that a changeling might enter his or her own pledge directly with the season, in much the same way that the Court founders did when they first created the Great Courts. Such an ordeal likely involves an arduous quest through the Hedge or some similarly significant trial, but it can be done \u2014 and changelings who are, for whatever reason, not welcome in polite freehold society have all the more reason to try.<br /> <br /> Bear this in mind when looking at the statistics for the sample antagonists throughout this section. Just because a ravening privateer is listed as belonging to a Court doesn\u2019t mean he\u2019ll be showing up at the society ball any time soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-13-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T17:12:03-07:00","id":299487,"title":"","content":"Tank you, kind <b>Satchel</b>, oh Great Librarian! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So here is next question: <b>What about of <i>idea</i> of Courts and connection with Seasons - from where new changelings can get them?</b> If they need to find, say, a Spring in the Hedge, were would they get the idea for that? Are Hobgoblins aware of that connection and can tell characters? Are True Fae and could they remember that their Keeper babbling something about &quot;those free rebels are joining the Autumn&quot;? Where are some books or items of changelings knowledge? In other way - <b>how <i>tradition</i> of Courts is passed in setting, beside the oral storytelling of Lost?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-01-2014, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T17:48:52-07:00","id":299508,"title":"","content":"One of the side effects of forging a Court is that the founder has a permanent and deliberately unbreakable lesser alliance pledge with the phenomenon and feels compelled to promote their Court; considering even the least-fae changeling has about a decade longer to work with than a mortal would, there's certainly time to build up a marketing base.<br /> <br /> On the less esoteric end of things, Tom Hood brought the Seasonal Courts to Miami from Europe in the form of his own initiation into the Autumn Court and ancient books of mystical-philosophical theory that he used to initiate Rose Thorne and Grandfather Thunder into the Spring and Summer Courts (and which La Llorona stole to begin Miami's Winter Court).<br /> <br /> And on the most abstract level, we're talking about crazy people with an innate connection to Fate's daughtermom - if a Court already exists, it's entirely possible that some delusion or other might lead a Courtless wayward to sign on for the hard sell with the Black Tortoise or the Iron Spear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T19:51:18-07:00","id":299546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=299109#post299109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2: The season automatically chooses the monarch, but the people involved must consent. Once the crown is granted, it must be given up by an act of will, whereupon it disappears and immediately appears upon the head of the next monarch, who may deny it if he wishes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always viewed that the Seasons choose the changeling that represents said season the best. Ero, the angriest person in the room is Summer, the most desirable is Spring, etc, etc. What the kicker is that the seasons can change this at a moments notice. The Summer king is only a king until another person who exemplifies Summer's ideals shows up in which the crown transfers to the new girl until the former king can out do the new Summer queen. <br /> <br /> As you can see, such a system naturally caters to the extremes which I like.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T23:34:58-07:00","id":299757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=299508#post299508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the side effects of forging a Court is that the founder has a permanent and deliberately unbreakable lesser alliance pledge with the phenomenon and feels compelled to promote their Court; considering even the least-fae changeling has about a decade longer to work with than a mortal would, there's certainly time to build up a marketing base.<br /> <br /> On the less esoteric end of things, Tom Hood brought the Seasonal Courts to Miami from Europe in the form of his own initiation into the Autumn Court and ancient books of mystical-philosophical theory that he used to initiate Rose Thorne and Grandfather Thunder into the Spring and Summer Courts (and which La Llorona stole to begin Miami's Winter Court).<br /> <br /> And on the most abstract level, we're talking about crazy people with an innate connection to Fate's daughtermom - if a Court already exists, it's entirely possible that some delusion or other might lead a Courtless wayward to sign on for the hard sell with the Black Tortoise or the Iron Spear.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are all good ideas, and really show me were the Courts come from. But still don't answer me main question: <b>If we have proto-freehold area with no Court or changling association, only the Lost PCs themselves - is there a way for them to get idea of the Courts? Could Seasons send some emissaries to them? Could PCs find books describing the Courts in mortals stuff? Could they Keeper knew about the Courts and would slip away in the time in Arcadia?</b><br /> <br /> All you say, for now, that changelings get idea of Courts from previous freeholds - and what about idea they don't know any other freehold or Lost, for that matter?<br /> <br /> I could envision that decades or even hundreds years before in area there were changelings, but now they are all hunt down by the PCs Keeper - the Arcadian Huntsman (see <b>CtL</b> corebook). Coming to think about, he could let PCs just get enough clues for them in Arcadia to get idea of the Courts, so they would rebuild Lost's freehold when they escape and make real Wild Hunt prize for him in the long time. Like athletes want to compete with the best possible rivals, Huntsman would let them become all powerful Lost only to come year later and crush them in their prime. Oh, such a devious idea I got... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-02-2014, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T03:00:49-08:00","id":301994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=299757#post299757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we have proto-freehold area with no Court or changling association, only the Lost PCs themselves - is there a way for them to get idea of the Courts? Could Seasons send some emissaries to them? Could PCs find books describing the Courts in mortals stuff? Could they Keeper knew about the Courts and would slip away in the time in Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just off the top of my head:<ul><li>The PCs have dreams with a strong seasonal and cyclic symbolism. Research into the subject (goblin-based, probably) reveals the existence of a vanished freehold.</li> <li>They find books penned by changelings in one of those weird little bookstores, offhandedly mentioning the Courts.</li> <li>A [seasonally appropriate animal] leads them to a seasonal almost-place at the edge of reality \u2013 a frozen pond in the middle of summer, a great autumn-red maple in winter, <i>et cetera</i> \u2013 where names are written. Signing on grants them a subtle dot in Mantle.</li> <li>An old stele tells them \u2013 straight-up <i>tells</i> them, with a voice and everything \u2013 about a community of Lost who were, but are no longer, and the crowns and cloaks they wore.</li> <li>Over time, they find indications of changelings that came before. They notice signs and marks only they can see, find hedgespun clothes in old wardrobes, see impossible flowers growing out of graves. Research, as above, is the key.</li> </ul><br /> Obviously, you could combine any of the above into a coherent narrative. You could do the &quot;signs of before&quot; thing, and have their research lead them to the standing stone, which in turns gives them enough information to locate the signing-places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T03:45:58-08:00","id":302009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=301994#post301994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A [seasonally appropriate animal] leads them to a seasonal almost-place at the edge of reality \u2013 a frozen pond in the middle of summer, a great autumn-red maple in winter, <i>et cetera</i> \u2013 where names are written. Signing on grants them a subtle dot in Mantle.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Hedge, yes? And wouldn't those places be connected to the seasons - so red maple shouldn't be in the Autumn based woods, with red and yellow leaves?<br /> <br /> And are there any canonical animals associations with Courts?<br /> <b>Update: </b>I see there are animals associated with Seasons in the Courts description Heraldy section in corebook. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=301994#post301994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over time, they find indications of changelings that came before. They notice signs and marks only they can see, find hedgespun clothes in old wardrobes, see impossible flowers growing out of graves. Research, as above, is the key.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was that from the time of the colonization, it weren't any freehold in area, because of Arcadian Huntsman, that is Keeper of PCs. Previously were <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/299763-native-american-changelings\">Native American freeholds</a> in the place, but long ago, at least 500 years. I could point a small changelings settlement here about, maybe 200-300 years ago - but I would want to at least mark total vanishing of it, probably because of Huntsman's Wild Hunts on previous freeholds members. &quot;Nothing lasted, their all gone!&quot; should be PCs reactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":".  Added Seasons Animals section 11-04-2014, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:43:40-08:00","id":302702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=302009#post302009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Hedge, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want. I was thinking more dreamlike, less <i>material\u200b</i>, though.<br /> That tree might be atop a tall building on our side of the Hedge, invisible from the ground; the frozen lake might be found in the apartment of the recently deceased, their possessions beneath the ice, and then be gone forever after the signing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T19:37:18-08:00","id":302876,"title":"","content":"They could also find information in a local Goblin Market (which has the benefit of more plot potential in exactly what the Hobs would *charge* for such information). Maybe there's a book, tapestry, or something else describing the seasonal courts in a Goblin's stall - one that draws the eye and interest of the players. When asked about it, the Hob explains just enough to pique their interest - there are great, ancient organizations that protect the Lost and grant them further power to protect themselves. It offers even more information - if the players &lt;insert quest here&gt;.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps there's a Hedge Beast or friendly hobgoblin that used to work with/for the native Lost and knows something of the Courts, or migrated from another Freehold after the Autumn King went crazy and sold everyone to the Viscount of Chains. It can explain the basics and work them through swearing their vows to the Seasons, but first they need to &lt;insert quest here&gt;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T01:33:58-08:00","id":303099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=302876#post302876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could also find information in a local Goblin Market (which has the benefit of more plot potential in exactly what the Hobs would *charge* for such information). Maybe there's a book, tapestry, or something else describing the seasonal courts in a Goblin's stall - one that draws the eye and interest of the players. When asked about it, the Hob explains just enough to pique their interest - there are great, ancient organizations that protect the Lost and grant them further power to protect themselves. It offers even more information - if the players &lt;insert quest here&gt;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea for &quot;I have findings of long lost organization that couple centuries ago vanished from this lands&quot; - very much thanks for idea! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Aren't Goblin Markets come to be <b>if</b> there are changelings nearby to come to them? Because with mine &quot;there is no freehold&quot; idea, it can be tough to pass it in-setting...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=302876#post302876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or perhaps there's a Hedge Beast or friendly hobgoblin that used to work with/for the native Lost and knows something of the Courts, or migrated from another Freehold after the Autumn King went crazy and sold everyone to the Viscount of Chains. It can explain the basics and work them through swearing their vows to the Seasons, but first they need to &lt;insert quest here&gt;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, this is even better! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But who is Viscount of Chains?<br /> <br /> I probably will go with &quot;Seasonal dreams&quot;, that are journeys to the &quot;other places&quot; from The MG's ideas to pique they interest. Unveiling the memory of they Keepers mentioning something about Seasons and Courts. And then let the players found their Courts pledge on the Goblin Market, or in the hobgoblins help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T19:22:36-08:00","id":304010,"title":"","content":"Goblin Markets can exist independently of the Lost. they're attended by hobgoblins, True Fae, the occasional mage or foolish human that wandered in... A freehold and a goblin market don't need to coexist. <br /> <br /> The Viscount of Chains is a Keeper I just made up. :P <br /> <br /> I'd avoid having the Courts as concepts passed down by the Keepers, as part of the reason the courts help protect you from the Others is that They *can't* understand the court systems. Maybe there were recaptured Lost in their Keepers' dungeons that moaned about their courtmates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T20:51:53-08:00","id":304122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=304010#post304010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd avoid having the Courts as concepts passed down by the Keepers, as part of the reason the courts help protect you from the Others is that They *can't* understand the court systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gentry can't understand <i>how</i> the magic of the Courts keeps them away. They're amply capable of understanding that the Courts exist in plural and inexplicably refrain from singularly trying to hold all the power in an area all of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T22:10:29-08:00","id":304195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/298980-\u200bhow-seasons-communicate-with-the-lost?p=304122#post304122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gentry can't understand <i>how</i> the magic of the Courts keeps them away. They're amply capable of understanding that the Courts exist in plural and inexplicably refrain from singularly trying to hold all the power in an area all of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that being all about hunting for sport - the Arcadian Huntsman from corebook - would like to make &quot;experiment&quot;, and rouse changelings society, only to test his strengths in confrontation with Lost with real magic. This why he would mention this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T05:20:59-08:00","id":401762,"title":"","content":"Returning to my previous idea - on next our game, near the Eastern, I want to make a founding of Courts for freehold. And by this, to put the competing PCs from the same Courts for the Crown on it. So two Summer-to-be changelings will probably fight for it. Spring-to-be Lost will compete in making the better fest. And a like.<br /> <br /> <b>Is this competition of &quot;I'm better embedding Court idea&quot;, good for choosing the Courts Monarch?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T10:17:46-08:00","id":402008,"title":"","content":"How courts work and which ones are available and concepts functions behind them are changing so keep that in mind. <br /> <br /> Personally the way I see it, the Seasons are Platonic Ideals or Universals, that the founders of the seasonal courts made a deal with. They don't have a consciousness like humans, but certain actions and things resonate with them and other things are the opposite and that's how Changelings commicate with the seasons, by doing things that resonate with the Ideal.<br /> <br /> Does anyone get what I'm saying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}